function about() {
  return `${header('A CLEARER WAY TO RESEARCH.', 'Good research starts<br>with <em>better questions.</em>', 'Alpha’s market context. Vision’s company perspective. One considered workspace.')}<div class="about-grid"><section class="panel prose"><span class="eyebrow">THE IDEA</span><h2>Go from the big picture<br>to your own point of view.</h2><p>ApexPro brings together a market overview, a searchable company universe, readable financial evidence and a private research journal. It is built for understanding Indian equities, not for executing trades.</p><h3>Where the numbers come from</h3><p>Company fundamentals, screen metrics and annual statements are served from Alpha’s published dataset. Market quotes and split-adjusted chart history come from Yahoo Finance through Tripwire’s existing data service. Each view names its data date. Quotes may be delayed; a recent fetch is not proof of a recent trade.</p><h3>How the checks work</h3><p>Uptrend means close above the 50-day moving average, with the 50-day above the 200-day. Quality screens require ROCE of at least 20% and operating cash flow of at least 1× profit. Value & quality requires positive P/E up to 20 and ROCE of at least 15%. These are fixed research filters, not forecasts.</p><p>Sector weather uses the median available one-month return; tile size shows company coverage. Breadth uses only names with both a valid close and 200-day average. Composite scores are supplied by Alpha; they are a research sorting aid, not an expected return. Financial comparisons need sector context, especially for banks and insurers.</p><h3>Missing and old data</h3><p>Missing numbers appear as a dash. A failed feed gets an explicit retry state. Offline responses are marked as cached; they may be old. Always confirm a material figure against the company’s filings and the exchange.</p></section><div><section class="panel prose"><span class="eyebrow">MAKE IT FEEL AT HOME</span><h2>Your research app.</h2><p>Install ApexPro for a dedicated window and quick access from your home screen.</p><button class="button" data-action="install">${icon('download')} Install ApexPro</button><p>On iPhone or iPad: open in Safari, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen. On Mac Safari: File → Add to Dock. In Chrome or Edge, use the install icon in the address bar.</p><p>The app shell works offline after your first visit. Previously accessed data may be available from cache; fresh research needs a connection.</p></section><section class="panel prose"><h3>Privacy & your research</h3><p>Watchlists, notes and theme preference are stored on your device. They are not sent to an account server. Export a backup from My Desk before clearing browser storage. Hosting and data providers may process request metadata such as IP addresses.</p><h3>Research, not advice</h3><p>ApexPro is an educational tool. It does not provide personalized investment advice, place orders, or promise returns. No SEBI registration is claimed. Verify information independently and consult a qualified adviser where appropriate.</p><p>Built by Akshay. <a href="https://askakshay.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit askakshay.com ${icon('arrow')}</a></p></section></div></div>`;
}
